WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.900
Six planets around HD 110,067 orbit in exact resonance, preserving the configuration they held at formation. This is Fascinating Frontiers, episode 242. University of Washington's life-free Earth model, space x's Starfall capsule, and November sky-watching notes follow, along with a cosmic deep dive. The star sits roughly 100 light years away, and universe space tech reports the innermost world completes an orbit in 9.11 days.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.880
The second planet takes 13.67 days, and the third takes 20.52 days.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.840
The European Space Agency's Chi-Ops Telescope supplied the data that revealed the pattern

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.240
after tests had spotted initial transits in 2020.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.340
Researchers use the resonance to predict and then verify three additional outer planets

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.500
whose orbits matched earlier anomalies in the star's brightness.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:57.100
Only about 1% of planetary systems retain this original resonance state after billions

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.540
of years. Each world is smaller than Neptune and carries a thick gaseous envelope resembling

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.780
those of Uranus or Neptune. The system's brightness makes it the most prominent known example

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:13.120
containing four or more planets, positioning it as a prime target for atmospheric study with

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:19.620
the James Webb Space Telescope, or JWST. Astronomers want to determine whether these planets are

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:25.400
rocky worlds with exceptionally thick atmospheres, or whether solid surfaces with liquid water oceans

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:31.357
exists beneath the clouds. University of Washington researchers built a virtual Earth model that

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:38.077
runs geochemical exchanges among core, mantle, crust, surface, and atmosphere for five billion years

00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:44.297
while excluding any biological influence. The Times of India reports the simulation reproduces 19

00:01:44.297 --> 00:01:50.717
observed planetary properties, including mantle heat flow. Lead author Samantha Gilbert Janasek

00:01:50.717 --> 00:01:55.617
completed the work as a doctoral student and is now a postdoctoral fellow at UC Riverside.

00:01:56.037 --> 00:02:00.497
She added surface and atmosphere modeling to an existing framework developed in senior

00:02:00.497 --> 00:02:02.097
author Rory Barnes' lab.

00:02:02.737 --> 00:02:07.757
The model can now be applied to any rocky exoplanet to test whether an observed atmosphere could

00:02:07.757 --> 00:02:08.837
arise without life.

00:02:09.377 --> 00:02:14.617
If the model fails to match the data, the mismatch strengthens the case for biological activity.

00:02:15.137 --> 00:02:19.077
The work was published in the Planetary Science Journal on September 18th.

00:02:19.077 --> 00:02:24.963
SpaceX opened a public page that lists Starfall's commercial specifications for the first time.

00:02:25.483 --> 00:02:31.363
Tesla Rade reports, each mission can carry up to 1,000 kilograms, supply 1 kilowatt

00:02:31.363 --> 00:02:35.983
of power, and maintain continuous starlink connectivity for real-time data return.

00:02:36.463 --> 00:02:41.543
The service targets biomedical customers who can grow stem cell organoids and replacement

00:02:41.543 --> 00:02:46.423
tissue, pharmaceutical companies working on protein and small molecule drug crystals,

00:02:46.423 --> 00:02:51.303
chemicals, and material science users growing semiconductors in vacuum and microgravity.

00:02:51.743 --> 00:02:55.263
Three commercial flights have already been booked and will launch on Starship.

00:02:55.863 --> 00:03:02.583
The capsule measures about 10.2 feet wide and 2.5 feet tall, and can return 2,200 pounds

00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:03.163
of cargo.

00:03:03.863 --> 00:03:08.923
President Gwynne Schottwell described the capsule as providing routine, relatively low-cost

00:03:08.923 --> 00:03:14.123
access to microgravity environments for scientific research, including improving understanding

00:03:14.123 --> 00:03:19.503
of diseases like cancer and diabetes. The first flight occurred in June and the second on the

00:03:19.503 --> 00:03:25.699
bandwagon 5 ride-share in October. Raquel Villanueva of the National Aeronautics and Space

00:03:25.699 --> 00:03:32.459
Administration, or NASA, Jet Propulsion Laboratory presented the monthly sky-watching tips. The southern

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:38.419
tarads peak around November 5th and the northern tarads around November 12th, each offering a chance

00:03:38.419 --> 00:03:43.919
of bright fireballs, though producing only a handful of meteors per hour under ideal conditions.

00:03:44.479 --> 00:03:50.319
Mars and Jupiter appear 1.2 degrees apart in the Predon sky on November 15th and 16th,

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:56.479
with Jupiter the brighter point and reddish Mars nearby. Voyager 1 reaches one light day from Earth

00:03:56.479 --> 00:04:02.079
on November 17th, meaning a signal at the speed of light takes 24 hours to reach the spacecraft

00:04:02.079 --> 00:04:04.619
wrapped, and another 24 hours for a reply.

00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:10.419
The Leonids peak on November 17th and 18th after Moon set, potentially producing up to

00:04:10.419 --> 00:04:13.079
15 meteors per hour under ideal conditions.

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:19.339
A supermoon rises on November 24th, the first of three consecutive supermoons, and may appear

00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:21.719
larger near the horizon due to the Moon illusion.

00:04:22.705 --> 00:04:27.645
The four member crew health and performance exploration analog crew exited their habitat

00:04:27.645 --> 00:04:32.565
on October 31 after completing a simulated Mars mission, according to NASA.

00:04:32.965 --> 00:04:37.185
The crew posed outside for the first time in more than a year following the end of their

00:04:37.185 --> 00:04:38.265
year-long isolation.

00:04:39.324 --> 00:04:45.064
The eight UER-MS-3 CubeSat established an optical link with a ground station only weeks after

00:04:45.064 --> 00:04:47.264
commissioning, Fizz.org reports.

00:04:47.904 --> 00:04:53.064
The demonstration used optical terminals developed by Lithuanian company Astrolite and was

00:04:53.064 --> 00:04:54.304
supported by ESA.

00:04:54.304 --> 00:04:59.664
The successful link marks a step in validating optical communications on small satellites,

00:05:00.184 --> 00:05:02.084
despite the complexity of the operation.

00:05:03.266 --> 00:05:09.206
JWST observations of interstellar comet 3i Atlas are supplying fresh data on the conditions

00:05:09.206 --> 00:05:13.726
under which the object formed around another star, space.com reports.

00:05:14.286 --> 00:05:19.926
The findings provide another clue toward understanding the origins of 3i Atlas and the planet forming

00:05:19.926 --> 00:05:21.486
conditions around other stars.

00:05:21.486 --> 00:05:27.352
High-rise images show that water ice frost in Martian polar craters changes location

00:05:27.352 --> 00:05:31.772
and thickness with the seasons, behaving differently even in neighboring craters because

00:05:31.772 --> 00:05:35.192
of local slopes and rim heights, Fizz.org reports.

00:05:35.892 --> 00:05:41.192
Mars shares many landforms and weather patterns with Earth, including changing seasons, yet

00:05:41.192 --> 00:05:46.472
its North polar ice cap is composed only of water, while the southern cap is carbon dioxide.

00:05:46.472 --> 00:05:52.692
side. Fine grain material preserved in asteroid Ryugu and similar meteorites reveals that water

00:05:52.692 --> 00:05:58.312
altered minerals extensively, yet left some primitive chemistry intact. The pattern suggests

00:05:58.312 --> 00:06:04.512
localized rather than uniform aqueous processing inside the parent bodies. These rocks are considered

00:06:04.512 --> 00:06:08.872
chemically primitive because they preserve the chemical composition of the early solar system

00:06:08.872 --> 00:06:15.338
remarkably well, while also reacting extensively with water after formation. In brief, Hubble

00:06:15.338 --> 00:06:20.178
has mapped an extended structure spanning 93 billion miles in a nearby star system,

00:06:20.538 --> 00:06:22.238
whose nature remains under study.

00:06:22.818 --> 00:06:28.798
Siteg Daily reports, J-W-S-T data point to young massive star clusters at high red shift

00:06:28.798 --> 00:06:33.658
as possible birthplaces of intermediate mass black hole seeds, according to Universe

00:06:33.658 --> 00:06:34.018
today.

00:06:35.134 --> 00:06:40.074
Six metronomes placed on a single table can swing at different speeds yet stay locked, so

00:06:40.074 --> 00:06:44.114
that every sixth swing of the slowest exactly matches the fastest ones count.

00:06:44.114 --> 00:06:48.954
That coordination mirror is an unbroken chain of simple whole-number orbital ratios.

00:06:49.474 --> 00:06:53.754
The pattern is the surviving signature of the gas and dust disk in which the planets

00:06:53.754 --> 00:06:54.114
grew.

00:06:54.774 --> 00:06:59.354
While the disk was still present, the planets migrated inward together, their mutual gravitational

00:06:59.354 --> 00:07:01.554
tugs keeping the resonance tight.

00:07:02.274 --> 00:07:04.714
Once the gas vanished, the chain froze in place.

00:07:05.414 --> 00:07:08.954
Any later giant impact or passing star would have broken the links.

00:07:09.494 --> 00:07:13.674
So the continued existence of the resonance tells us the system has experienced almost

00:07:13.674 --> 00:07:17.014
no violence since the disc dispersed billions of years ago.

00:07:17.887 --> 00:07:21.327
Most systems lose this delicate balance when giant planets form,

00:07:21.947 --> 00:07:25.367
neighboring stars tug on orbits or collisions scramble the arrangement.

00:07:26.007 --> 00:07:29.227
Here the planets apparently avoided every one of those disruptions,

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:31.967
leaving their original spacing frozen in place.

00:07:32.975 --> 00:07:35.075
Because the periods are known to high precision,

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:38.295
future transit observations can be timed exactly,

00:07:38.835 --> 00:07:42.175
allowing telescopes to catch every planet passing in front of the star

00:07:42.175 --> 00:07:43.635
without wasted pointings.

00:07:43.635 --> 00:07:49.095
Small deviations from perfect commensurability reveal the planet's masses through their gravitational

00:07:49.095 --> 00:07:50.635
influence on one another.

00:07:51.135 --> 00:07:56.295
Those masses, combined with radius measurements from the transit depth, yield bulk densities

00:07:56.295 --> 00:07:59.795
that already hint at substantial atmospheres rather than bare rock.

00:08:00.435 --> 00:08:05.095
The resonance therefore functions as a natural scale that converts timing data into physical

00:08:05.095 --> 00:08:08.035
properties without requiring additional assumptions.

00:08:09.152 --> 00:08:14.072
Astronomers can now use the known periods to refine mass estimates and test whether any

00:08:14.072 --> 00:08:18.072
of the worlds retain substantial rocky cores beneath their thick envelopes.

00:08:18.652 --> 00:08:24.252
Targeted JWST spectroscopy is lined up to measure atmospheric composition and search

00:08:24.252 --> 00:08:29.212
for signs of the kind of chemical disequilibrium the whole Earth simulation is designed to flag.

00:08:29.872 --> 00:08:34.332
The precise timing provided by the resonance makes it an especially efficient target for

00:08:34.332 --> 00:08:38.332
follow-up observations that could distinguish between formation scenarios.

00:08:39.413 --> 00:08:43.173
Models show that resonant chains are common at formation but rare today.

00:08:43.773 --> 00:08:47.893
What protected this particular chain for billions of years while thousands of others were

00:08:47.893 --> 00:08:48.373
disrupted?

00:08:48.973 --> 00:08:53.293
The answer may lie in the absence of a gas giant that could have scattered the inner planets,

00:08:53.773 --> 00:08:58.253
or in the quiet stellar environment around HD 110,067.

00:08:58.773 --> 00:09:01.033
Either way, the system stands as a benchmark.

00:09:01.033 --> 00:09:06.793
Any theory of planet formation must now explain not only how resonances arise, but

00:09:06.793 --> 00:09:13.048
how a few of them endure across cosmic time. Watch the pre-Don sky on November 15th, when

00:09:13.048 --> 00:09:18.808
Mars and Jupiter share the same frame, and on November 17th, when Voyager 1's radio weight

00:09:18.808 --> 00:09:24.508
stretches to a full day each way. That covers today's Space and Science news. Share this

